cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this thesis, its simulator, or its data, please cite it as below."
type: software
title: "Cloud GPU Rendering Scheduling Problem (CGRSP): A Mathematical Formulation and Empirical Evaluation on Heterogeneous GPU Fleets"
abstract: >-
  This thesis formulates the Cloud GPU Rendering Scheduling Problem (CGRSP):
  assigning batch 3D rendering jobs, one frame per job, to heterogeneous
  on-demand GPUs under uncertain node availability and mixed deadlines. A
  Python discrete-event simulator is calibrated on 6,234 recorded RunPod
  Serverless jobs and compares ten scheduling policies across four experimental
  phases. The deposit contains the thesis source and PDF, the simulator, the
  calibration data, the simulation outputs, the generated tables and figures,
  and a one-command reproduction script. It also contains the classical and
  learned baseline experiments and the fleet-composition sweep added for the
  journal version.
